# Supply-chain hardening: only install package versions published more than
# 7 days ago, giving compromised releases time to be detected/yanked. npm
# applies this as a `before` cutoff. The functions package is resolved with its
# own project config (npm uses the nearest package root), so this mirrors the
# repo-root .npmrc and the Dependabot `cooldown` in .github/dependabot.yml.
min-release-age=7

# Narrow exemption from the cooldown above, matching the frontend's .npmrc: a
# security fix published inside the window, where waiting means shipping the
# advisory. Only the named package is exempt — its own dependencies still follow
# the policy. Delete this once the cooldown has caught up with it.
#
# follow-redirects: reached through `axios`. 1.16.1 and earlier leak credential
# headers across origins (GHSA-q3jh-wrc6-jgq8, GHSA-8r9p-f939-6h3c,
# GHSA-mrwp-f3q8-3g9p); the fix is 1.16.2.
min-release-age-exclude[]=follow-redirects
